new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/grapheneos/vendor/worm/fonts/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# Worm OS local fonts
+
+Place locally licensed PragmataPro files here:
+
+```text
+local/PragmataPro-Regular.ttf
+local/PragmataPro-Bold.ttf
+local/PragmataProMono-Regular.ttf
+local/PragmataProMono-Bold.ttf
+```
+
+These font files are intentionally excluded from Git.
+
+Named Android font families:
+
+```text
+sans-serif -> PragmataPRO, then Roboto, then the original Android/GrapheneOS fallback chain
+monospace -> PragmataProMono, then DroidSansMono, then the original Android/GrapheneOS fallback chain
+worm-system-primary
+worm-system-monospace
+worm-ui -> worm-system-primary
+worm-mono -> worm-system-monospace
+worm-original-sans -> roboto
+```
+
+The fonts are packaged in the PRODUCT partition and therefore become part of signed Worm OS releases and OTA packages.
+
+The customization file only prepends Worm families inside Android's product
+font customization mechanism. It does not replace or remove the framework
+fonts.xml default fallback list, Noto language coverage, CJK fallback, or emoji
+fonts.
+
+The build only defines and packages font modules for files that are present locally. Missing bold weights are reported by `check-fonts.sh`; until local bold files are supplied and wired into `Android.bp` and `config/fonts_customization.xml`, Android synthesizes requested bold/intermediate weights from the available regular files.

